1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,969
AI can call a football match.

2
00:00:02,009 --> 00:00:03,502
Can it prove what it says?

3
00:00:03,542 --> 00:00:07,510
CRONISTA: a multi-agent broadcast where
every sentence is traceable.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,063
Two LLM coaches, GPT-6 Astra and
GPT-6.1 Sol, manage the teams.

5
00:00:13,103 --> 00:00:18,510
A shared engine resolves the play; a desk
of three voices narrates it.

6
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:24,288
Narrator (pre-match presentation): Welcome to the arena:
Atlético Puertoscuro against Olímpico Nebrisa.

7
00:00:25,033 --> 00:00:30,929
Narrator (pre-match presentation): Atlético Puertoscuro line up
in a four-two-three-one, with GPT-6 Astra in charge.

8
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:34,243
While the coaches decide, the clock waits.

9
00:00:34,283 --> 00:00:38,970
Both see the same committed state and return a
validated JSON plan for every player.

10
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:50,272
Narrator (goal call): What a goal! Ismael Barido, goal!
Olímpico Nebrisa level it, one–one, after 52 seconds.

11
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:53,741
The commentator may only analyse with a cited fact.

12
00:00:53,781 --> 00:00:55,656
Eight deterministic rules check it;

13
00:00:55,696 --> 00:00:58,940
a failure is retried once, then becomes a labelled template.

14
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:03,038
Team and player numbers come from the
engine's events and frames:

15
00:01:03,078 --> 00:01:06,320
passes, shots, distance and top speed in kilometres per hour.

16
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:07,827
Make it yours:

17
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:13,001
star a club and a player, follow only that player,
and choose a fan, analyst or player view.

18
00:01:13,041 --> 00:01:14,800
Spanish switches text and voice.

19
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:19,040
Narrator in Spanish: «Final del partido. Atlético…»

20
00:01:19,690 --> 00:01:25,073
A versioned Microsoft Foundry agent answers questions
with read-only tools over the confirmed play.

21
00:01:25,113 --> 00:01:27,100
Its sentences pass the same verifier.

22
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:29,548
The six models also play each other.

23
00:01:29,588 --> 00:01:33,810
Every league match has a replay, and the page
states what the results cannot prove.

24
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:37,432
The same verifier guards the automated match report:

25
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:41,500
click any sentence to see its events, or
open every draft and verdict.

26
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:47,140
All data is synthetic: a documented dataset,
and JSON for broadcast overlays.

27
00:01:47,730 --> 00:01:54,038
It runs on Azure OpenAI, Foundry, Speech and Container
Apps, with over three thousand automated checks.

28
00:01:54,078 --> 00:01:57,120
CRONISTA: narrate the match, prove every sentence.
